{"text": "For decades, companies have treated data like a sealed box ― valuable, private, and tightly protected. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That instinct made sense. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> What was inside the box ― customer histories, operational insights, proprietary knowledge ― represented control and competitive advantage. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In an industrial economy, owning data was power. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But in the Intelligence Age, that logic is becoming an obstacle. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Value no longer comes primarily from keeping information but from connecting it ― across functions, partners, and ecosystems ― to enable learning and action in real time. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Holding on to the sealed box today is less like safeguarding an asset and more like dragging an anchor. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The companies moving fastest are not just opening the box. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> They are doing something more deliberate, opening it just enough to allow data to move, combine, and learn ― securely, selectively, and with purpose. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The objective is not openness for its own sake but smart connection to gain an edge.", "alignment": {"characters": ["F", "o", "r", " ", "d", "e", "c", "a", "d", "e", "s", ",", " ", "c", "o", "m", "p", "a", "n", "i", "e", "s", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "t", "r", "e", "a", "t", "e", "d", " ", "d", "a", "t", "a", " ", "l", "i", "k", "e", " ", "a", " ", "s", "e", "a", "l", "e", "d", " ", "b", "o", "x", " ", "―", " ", "v", "a", "l", "u", "a", "b", "l", "e", ",", " ", "p", "r", "i", "v", "a", "t", "e", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "i", "g", "h", "t", "l", "y", " ", "p", "r", "o", "t", "e", "c", "t", "e", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "a", "t", " ", "i", "n", "s", "t", "i", "n", "c", "t", " ", "m", "a", "d", "e", " ", "s", "e", "n", "s", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", 